.idea/
.vscode/
**/__pycache__/
**/.DS_Store
/mlruns/
/.cmdstan/
**/lightning_logs/
# Legacy: nothing writes output.log since Step 5 dropped the `basicConfig(filename=...)` sink (the console is now the
# only one). Kept so a stale file from before that change stays untracked -- untracking it would make it show up in
# `git ls-files --others`, which the lazy cache keys on. Safe to delete the file, then this line.
/output.log
/outputs/
**/*.db
/job_scripts/

# Per-user, per-machine paths -- see .env.example, which IS tracked. Never commit .env: it is the one file that is
# legitimately different on every machine, so a committed copy is a merge conflict on every clone.
/.env

# Coverage / pytest artifacts. `.coverage` is a SQLite database rewritten by every pytest run, and the lazy cache
# keys on `git diff HEAD` over the WHOLE repo -- so while it was tracked, having run the tests since the last commit
# changed the cache key and could redo (or skip) a ~20 GiB prepare. Untracked in the block 4g opening commit; see
# .claude/plans/step-4-stages.md.
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
